 "demo": [
  {
   "time": "0:00",
   "text": "This is XFed-IDS. Ten organisations trained this detector together without sharing traffic. The flows on the left are validation rows replayed as live traffic, never test rows.",
   "sources": [
    "PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "0:30",
   "text": "Top row: our preregistered FedAvgM model's test macro-F1, 0.9852 at α=0.5, scored once. Per-flow latency 45.7 µs with ONNX. Upload per round falls 50% with fp16 updates. Each number links to the file it came from.",
   "sources": [
    "results/federated_methods/test_once/result.json",
    "results/efficiency/inference_speed_summary.json",
    "docs/efficiency_results.md",
    "PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "1:00",
   "text": "The model says DoS. On the right is why: SHAP shows which features pushed it there, here packet-length statistics. Base value, output and residual are shown, because SHAP's sums aren't exact and we measured that.",
   "sources": []
  },
  {
   "time": "1:30",
   "text": "This sentence is an LLM summary for the analyst. It is labelled 'not a research result': a usability feature, not a research claim.",
   "sources": []
  },
  {
   "time": "1:50",
   "text": "We don't hide mistakes. Here is a flow the model got wrong.",
   "sources": []
  },
  {
   "time": "2:15",
   "text": "This is the trust check, a separate experiment. Open circle: how often our agent flagged each organisation with no attack. Filled: under attack. At seed 1337, org 5 goes from 0.00 to 0.95: real detection. But some orgs are flagged in almost every round with no attack at all; the note under the chart names them. That is the compositional confound.",
   "sources": [
    "docs/contribution_b_results.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "3:00",
   "text": "Investigate answers four questions, trust first. Multi-Krum excluded a poisoned org 0% of the time. ByzAgent's result, in our locked words: [read the quote on screen].",
   "sources": [
    "docs/contribution_b_results.md",
    "PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "3:40",
   "text": "Explanation check. Chance is 0.065, the seed-noise floor is 0.429. At α=5.0 agreement is 0.667; at α=0.1 it is 0.333, below the floor: directional, not significant, the intervals overlap.",
   "sources": [
    "docs/contribution_a_results.md",
    "PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "4:20",
   "text": "1,587,920 bytes per round; compression saves up to 74.9% of upload with no detectable effect at n=3; and two ideas we tested and dropped.",
   "sources": [
    "results/efficiency/communication.json",
    "docs/efficiency_results.md",
    "PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "4:40",
   "text": "Finally, Limits shows our claims and limitations verbatim from the project instructions. We'd rather you read them here than find them yourself.",
   "sources": []
  },
  {
   "time": "5:00",
   "text": "Back to the slides for what we checked and what failed.",
   "sources": []
  }
 ]
